#### 15. **CertificateToolTests.java:1197-1210** — Test passes `--ca-keyusage` with empty string, but `getCaKeyUsage` treats empty string as default
```java
final String caKeyUsage = randomFrom("", Strings.collectionToCommaDelimitedString(CertificateTool.DEFAULT_CA_KEY_USAGE));
...
"--ca-keyusage", caKeyUsage
```
```java
// CertificateTool.java:330-340
final List<String> getCaKeyUsage(OptionSet options) {
    if (options.has(caKeyUsageSpec)) {
        String rawCaKeyUsage = caKeyUsageSpec.value(options);
        if (Strings.isNullOrEmpty(rawCaKeyUsage)) {
            return DEFAULT_CA_KEY_USAGE;  // empty string → default
        }
        return List.of(Strings.splitStringByCommaToArray(rawCaKeyUsage));
    } else {
        return DEFAULT_CA_KEY_USAGE;
    }
}
```
**Failure scenario:** Test passes `--ca-keyusage ""` (empty string). `getCaKeyUsage` returns `DEFAULT_CA_KEY_USAGE`. Test expects this? The test doesn't assert keyUsage. But the **defect**: user explicitly passes `--ca-keyusage ""` intending "no keyUsage", but gets default. No way to disable KeyUsage for CA via CLI. Should allow empty to mean "no keyUsage extension".

